 use up the PostHog free-tier quota quickly and inflate the\n  funnel. Instead:\n  - the \"started\" events are de-duplicated with a flag,\n  - the slider uses `onChangeEnd`,\n  - scrolling uses `ScrollEndNotification`.\n\n  This works out to about one event per user action.\n- **PII.** No email or phone value is sent. The text fields only check whether\n  the value is non-empty.\n- **`terms` on continue.** The Continue button is only enabled when terms are\n  accepted, so `terms` will always be `true` in practice. I still send it\n  because the spec asks for it.\n- **Repeat events.** `loan_amount_changed`, `terms_accepted` and\n  `offers_scrolled` can fire more than once per visit if the user repeats the\n  action. That is intended: each one is a real interaction. Funnels should count\n  unique users rather than total events.\n- I didn't add any screen-view events, since `PosthogObserver` already tracks\n  those.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `dart format` and `flutter analyze` passed with no issues.\n- I didn't run the app or any tests (the repo has none), and I sent no events\n  anywhere.\n- `flutter pub get` created `pubspec.lock` and `.dart_tool/`, and\n  `flutter analyze` rewrote `analysis_options.yaml`. I reverted all three, so\n  the only changed files are the two screens and this file.\n\n## Worth flagging (not changed)\n\n- `Analytics.init` runs in every build, including debug. Once the real key is\n  added in CI, local and dev runs will also send events to the production\n  project and use up the free-tier quota. You could disable capture in\n  `kDebugMode`, or use a separate project key for dev.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0147EqHBk2zTUVb2PUUBHqwi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSAPcTZD8GgbZhFySmLp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the registration and offers screens, all sent through `Analytics.capture`. `flutter analyze` reports no issues. I haven't run the app (the repo has no tests), and nothing was sent to PostHog. The details are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**When each event fires.** I set it up so each user action sends about one event, because you're on PostHog's free tier. Hooking straight into the input callbacks would send an event on every keystroke, every slider movement and every scroll frame, which would use up the quota and skew the funnel.\n- **`registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started`:** once per visit to the screen, on the first character typed.\n- **`loan_amount_changed`:** once when the user lets go of the slider, with the final amount.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** only when the box goes from unticked to ticked.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped`:** right before moving to the offers screen, with `amount` and `terms`.\n- **`offers_scrolled`:** once each time a scroll comes to a stop, with how far the list has scrolled.\n\n**Other points:**\n- The email and phone number are never sent, only whether the field has something in it.\n- `terms` on the Continue event will always be `true`, because the button only becomes active once the terms are ticked. I still send it because the spec asks for it.\n- The amount, terms and scroll events can fire more than once per visit if the user repeats the action. Funnels should count unique users, not total events.\n- Running `flutter pub get` and `flutter analyze` created `pubspec.lock` and `.dart_tool/`, and changed `analysis_options.yaml`. I undid all three, so only the two screen files and `ANSWER.md` have changed.\n\n**Decision for you:** analytics also runs in debug builds. Once the real key is added in CI, local and dev runs will send events to the live project and use up the free-tier quota. I didn't change this; the fix is to turn analytics off in debug builds or use a separate key for dev.\n\nNothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1282,"cache_read_input_tokens":29034,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1282},"output_tokens":668,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d20ef1b-c310-4013-a70f-bf73dc2f7bef","uuid":"d59582a1-88d2-428e-bc8a-ff380427caf0","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:07:58.908Z","request_id":"req_011CgSAPcCRZ8v5RhPV5GAri"}
